1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:05,097
Someone who is sixteen point nine
years old says their age is sixteen.

2
00:00:05,097 --> 00:00:06,195
Not seventeen.

3
00:00:06,595 --> 00:00:08,578
Age counts completed years.

4
00:00:08,578 --> 00:00:14,042
Sixteen point one, sixteen point five,
sixteen point nine: all just sixteen.

5
00:00:14,492 --> 00:00:17,557
Diya saw this on the health
camp form at college.

6
00:00:17,907 --> 00:00:19,653
Rounding down looks easy.

7
00:00:19,653 --> 00:00:22,856
But what is minus two
point one, rounded down?

8
00:00:22,856 --> 00:00:24,813
Minus two, or minus three?

9
00:00:25,313 --> 00:00:27,440
Two special functions answer this.

10
00:00:27,440 --> 00:00:30,096
Signum, and the greatest integer function.

11
00:00:30,746 --> 00:00:33,290
First, signum, the Latin word for sign.

12
00:00:33,640 --> 00:00:35,022
It asks one thing.

13
00:00:35,022 --> 00:00:37,876
Is a number positive, negative, or zero?

14
00:00:38,276 --> 00:00:40,029
Positive x gives one.

15
00:00:40,029 --> 00:00:41,429
Zero gives zero.

16
00:00:41,429 --> 00:00:43,591
Negative x gives minus one.

17
00:00:43,991 --> 00:00:45,199
Watch x slide.

18
00:00:45,199 --> 00:00:47,285
Minus three gives minus one.

19
00:00:47,285 --> 00:00:49,648
Minus a half, still minus one.

20
00:00:49,648 --> 00:00:51,349
Only the sign matters.

21
00:00:51,749 --> 00:00:53,702
At zero, the output is zero.

22
00:00:53,702 --> 00:00:56,987
Just after zero, it jumps
to one, and stays there.

23
00:00:57,387 --> 00:01:00,353
Two flat rays and one dot at the origin.

24
00:01:00,353 --> 00:01:02,310
Domain: all real numbers.

25
00:01:02,310 --> 00:01:05,149
Range: just minus one, zero and one.

26
00:01:05,799 --> 00:01:08,895
NCERT also writes signum with the modulus.

27
00:01:08,895 --> 00:01:10,337
Mod x, over x.

28
00:01:10,737 --> 00:01:11,674
Step one.

29
00:01:11,674 --> 00:01:14,225
If x is five, mod x is five.

30
00:01:14,225 --> 00:01:16,113
Five over five is one.

31
00:01:16,863 --> 00:01:17,782
Step two.

32
00:01:17,782 --> 00:01:21,089
If x is minus five, mod x is still five.

33
00:01:21,089 --> 00:01:23,745
Five over minus five is minus one.

34
00:01:24,495 --> 00:01:25,540
Step three.

35
00:01:25,540 --> 00:01:30,397
At zero we cannot divide, so
signum of zero is defined as zero.

36
00:01:31,147 --> 00:01:33,364
Now the greatest integer function.

37
00:01:33,364 --> 00:01:36,053
We write it as x inside square brackets.

38
00:01:36,403 --> 00:01:40,987
Square bracket x means the greatest
integer that is less than or equal

39
00:01:40,987 --> 00:01:41,887
to x.

40
00:01:42,043 --> 00:01:46,298
List every integer not bigger
than x, then pick the largest one.

41
00:01:46,698 --> 00:01:48,160
Take two point seven.

42
00:01:48,160 --> 00:01:52,363
The integers not bigger than it
are two, one, zero, and so on.

43
00:01:52,363 --> 00:01:53,730
The largest is two.

44
00:01:54,130 --> 00:01:55,722
Now take exactly three.

45
00:01:55,722 --> 00:01:59,062
Three is allowed, so square
bracket three is three.

46
00:01:59,712 --> 00:02:00,612
Careful.

47
00:02:00,377 --> 00:02:02,730
Chopping off the decimal is different.

48
00:02:02,730 --> 00:02:05,091
For two point seven, both give two.

49
00:02:05,491 --> 00:02:08,519
For minus two point one,
chopping gives minus two.

50
00:02:08,519 --> 00:02:11,520
But minus two is to the
right, so it is bigger.

51
00:02:12,120 --> 00:02:13,060
Your turn.

52
00:02:13,060 --> 00:02:15,613
Square bracket minus two point one.

53
00:02:15,613 --> 00:02:17,721
Minus two, or minus three?

54
00:02:17,721 --> 00:02:19,106
Pause and decide.

55
00:02:22,306 --> 00:02:23,305
Minus three!

56
00:02:23,305 --> 00:02:25,911
It is the first integer to the left.

57
00:02:25,911 --> 00:02:28,126
Rounding down always moves left.

58
00:02:28,776 --> 00:02:29,824
Remember this.

59
00:02:29,824 --> 00:02:33,794
The greatest integer function
always rounds down, to the left.

60
00:02:34,494 --> 00:02:36,700
Now let x run, and draw the graph.

61
00:02:37,050 --> 00:02:41,592
From minus two up to minus one,
square bracket x stays at minus two.

62
00:02:41,992 --> 00:02:43,944
Then it is zero, then one.

63
00:02:43,944 --> 00:02:46,284
Each value holds flat, then jumps.

64
00:02:46,684 --> 00:02:48,347
The graph is a staircase.

65
00:02:48,347 --> 00:02:51,924
A filled dot starts each step,
and an empty dot ends it.

66
00:02:52,524 --> 00:02:54,853
Filled means that end is included.

67
00:02:54,853 --> 00:02:56,516
Empty means it is not.

68
00:02:56,916 --> 00:02:57,816
Step one.

69
00:02:57,763 --> 00:03:02,509
For x from zero up to one, but
not one, square bracket x is zero.

70
00:03:03,259 --> 00:03:04,159
Step two.

71
00:03:04,003 --> 00:03:07,338
For x from one up to two,
but not two, it is one.

72
00:03:08,088 --> 00:03:09,057
Step three.

73
00:03:09,057 --> 00:03:14,287
In general, if square bracket x is
n, then n is less than or equal to x,

74
00:03:14,287 --> 00:03:16,634
and x is less than n plus one.

75
00:03:17,384 --> 00:03:19,652
The domain is all real numbers.

76
00:03:19,652 --> 00:03:21,594
The range is the integers.

77
00:03:22,244 --> 00:03:23,144
Quick one.

78
00:03:23,064 --> 00:03:26,957
At x equal to two, is the
staircase at height one, or two?

79
00:03:26,957 --> 00:03:28,117
Pause and think.

80
00:03:31,317 --> 00:03:32,236
Height two!

81
00:03:32,236 --> 00:03:34,084
Square bracket two is two.

82
00:03:34,084 --> 00:03:36,502
The filled dot starts the new step.

83
00:03:37,152 --> 00:03:38,887
Now, one worked example.

84
00:03:39,237 --> 00:03:43,292
Solve two times square bracket
x, minus one, equals five.

85
00:03:43,792 --> 00:03:44,692
Step one.

86
00:03:44,624 --> 00:03:46,298
Add one to both sides.

87
00:03:46,298 --> 00:03:48,702
Two times square bracket x is six.

88
00:03:49,452 --> 00:03:50,374
Step two.

89
00:03:50,374 --> 00:03:51,645
Divide by two.

90
00:03:51,645 --> 00:03:53,725
Square bracket x is three.

91
00:03:54,475 --> 00:03:55,427
Step three.

92
00:03:55,427 --> 00:03:56,856
The staircase rule.

93
00:03:56,856 --> 00:04:01,091
Three is less than or equal
to x, and x is less than four.

94
00:04:01,841 --> 00:04:02,741
Step four.

95
00:04:02,711 --> 00:04:07,344
So x is any number from three,
included, up to four, not included.

96
00:04:08,094 --> 00:04:09,876
A whole step of answers.

97
00:04:09,876 --> 00:04:11,862
Three point nine nine works.

98
00:04:11,862 --> 00:04:13,013
Four does not.

99
00:04:13,663 --> 00:04:15,128
Now, the exam trap.

100
00:04:15,478 --> 00:04:18,339
Find square bracket
minus three point seven.

101
00:04:18,339 --> 00:04:21,300
Many students drop the
decimal: minus three.

102
00:04:21,700 --> 00:04:23,508
But minus three is bigger.

103
00:04:23,508 --> 00:04:25,620
Move left to the first integer.

104
00:04:25,620 --> 00:04:27,379
The answer is minus four.

105
00:04:28,029 --> 00:04:29,404
Where is it asked?

106
00:04:29,404 --> 00:04:33,786
JEE Main, in questions that build a
function from square bracket x and

107
00:04:33,786 --> 00:04:35,161
ask for its range.

108
00:04:35,761 --> 00:04:37,077
Exam level now.

109
00:04:37,077 --> 00:04:39,421
This function mixes both ideas.

110
00:04:39,421 --> 00:04:40,972
What is its range?

111
00:04:40,972 --> 00:04:42,345
Pause and solve.

112
00:04:47,745 --> 00:04:49,055
The answer is C.

113
00:04:49,055 --> 00:04:51,715
Minus two, minus one, zero and one.

114
00:04:52,215 --> 00:04:55,138
At x equal to zero, every part is zero.

115
00:04:55,638 --> 00:04:59,329
For any other integer, the
two brackets cancel to zero.

116
00:04:59,329 --> 00:05:02,272
So f is just the sign, one or minus one.

117
00:05:02,772 --> 00:05:07,163
For a number that is not an integer,
the two brackets add to minus one.

118
00:05:07,663 --> 00:05:11,952
So f is zero for positive x,
and minus two for negative x.

119
00:05:11,952 --> 00:05:15,166
Range: minus two, minus one, zero, one.

120
00:05:15,767 --> 00:05:17,229
Here is your recap.

121
00:05:17,229 --> 00:05:18,732
Screenshot this card.

122
00:05:21,932 --> 00:05:24,930
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

123
00:05:25,330 --> 00:05:26,230
One.

124
00:05:25,837 --> 00:05:28,191
What is the signum of minus seven?

125
00:05:28,191 --> 00:05:29,879
And the signum of zero?

126
00:05:30,779 --> 00:05:31,679
Two.

127
00:05:31,339 --> 00:05:34,378
Find square bracket minus zero point five.

128
00:05:35,278 --> 00:05:36,178
Three.

129
00:05:35,930 --> 00:05:39,784
For which numbers x is square
bracket x equal to five?

130
00:05:40,884 --> 00:05:44,526
Next time: one sheet of graph
paper, six different shapes.

131
00:05:44,526 --> 00:05:46,048
Can you name each one?

132
00:05:46,048 --> 00:05:47,837
Graphs of standard functions.
